OL,3,GNEWSARam sales go ahead despite
OL,4,Abluetongue disease restrictions nearby
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe biggest single-day ram sale in
OL,7,FEurope has begun in the Scottish
OL,8,FBorders despite disease restrictions
OL,9,Fimposed on much of neighbouring
OL,10,FDumfries and Galloway after cases of
OL,11,Fbluetongue were detected.
OL,13,FMore than 4,300 rams across 17 breeds
OL,14,Fwill go under the hammer in Kelso with
OL,15,Fmore than #5m expected to change hands.
OL,17,FA new restricted zone came into force
OL,18,Fin south-west Scotland on Thursday
OL,19,Fmeaning livestock such as cattle, sheep
OL,20,Fand other susceptible ruminants will
OL,21,Fstill need a licence if they are being
OL,22,Fmoved to the rest of Scotland.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
